{
 "content": [
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "A wonderful property of modern life is that we have anti-biotics to kill bacterial infections. However, we only have a fixed number of anti-biotic medicines, and bacteria are evolving to become resistent to our anti-biotics. In this example we are going to use probability to understand evolution of anti-biotic resistence in bacteria.",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "justify"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Imagine you have a population of 1 million infectious bacteria in your gut, 10% of which have a mutation that makes them slightly more resistant to anti-biotics. You take a course of anti-biotics. The probability that bacteria with the mutation survives is 20%. The probability that bacteria without the mutation survives is 1%.",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "justify"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "What is the probability that a randomly chosen bacterium survives the anti-biotics?",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
         },
         "type": "textStyle"
        }
       ],
       "text": "Let ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "E",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
         },
         "type": "textStyle"
        }
       ],
       "text": " be the event that our bacterium survives. Let ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "M",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
         },
         "type": "textStyle"
        }
       ],
       "text": " be the event that a bacteria has the mutation. By the ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "class": null,
          "href": "./law_total",
          "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow",
          "target": "_blank"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "Law of Total Probability",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
         },
         "type": "textStyle"
        }
       ],
       "text": " (LOTP):",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\t\\p(E) \n\t\t&= \\p(E \\and M) + \\p(E \\and M\\c)\n\t\t\t&& \\text{LOTP} \\\\ \n\t\t&= \\p(E | M)\\p(M) + \\p(E | M\\c)\\p(M\\c)\n\t\t\t&& \\text{Chain Rule} \\\\ \t\n\t\t&= 0.20 \\cdot 0.10 + 0.01 \\cdot 0.90 \n\t\t\t&& \\text{Substituting} \\\\ \n\t\t&= 0.029\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    }
   ],
   "type": "borderedBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "What is the probability that a surviving bacterium has the mutation?",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
         },
         "type": "textStyle"
        }
       ],
       "text": "Using the same events in the last section, this question is asking for ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "P(M|E)",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
         },
         "type": "textStyle"
        }
       ],
       "text": ". We aren't giving the conditional probability in that direction, instead we know ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "P(E|M)",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
         },
         "type": "textStyle"
        }
       ],
       "text": ". Such situations call for ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "class": null,
          "href": "./bayes_theorem",
          "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow",
          "target": "_blank"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "Bayes' Theorem",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
         },
         "type": "textStyle"
        }
       ],
       "text": ":",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\t\\p(M | E) \n\t\t&=  \\frac{\\p(E|M)\\p(M)}{\\p(E)} \n\t\t\t&& \\text{Bayes} \\\\\n\t\t&=  \\frac{0.20 \\cdot 0.10}{\\p(E)} \n\t\t\t&& \\text{Given} \\\\\n\t\t&=  \\frac{0.20 \\cdot 0.10}{0.029} \n\t\t\t&& \\text{Calculated} \\\\\n\t\t&\\approx  0.69\n\t\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    }
   ],
   "type": "borderedBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "color": "rgb(33, 37, 41)"
       },
       "type": "textStyle"
      }
     ],
     "text": "After the course of anti-biotics, 69% of bacteria have the mutation, up from 10% before. If this population is allowed to reproduce you will have a much more resistent set of bacteria!",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  }
 ],
 "type": "doc"
}
